From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] AI: silence only for the part of a field the DAC did not play

ai_deliver_frame pushed a whole field of silence whenever nothing new
had played since the last look at the play position. Samples handed over
earlier in the same field (AI_LEN reads, end of a DMA) did not count, so
a game polling AI_LEN got its audio plus a field of silence: Mischief
Makers (PAL) produced up to 595 frames for a 441-frame field and a
frontend pacing on audio ran it at about 44 of its 50 fps (130+ fps in
fast-forward, so not a speed problem).

Count what any path handed over during the field; while a transfer is
playing nothing is padded, and a DAC that ran dry gets silence only for
the rest of the field.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ai/ai_controller.h
+++ b/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ai/ai_controller.h
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@
     uint32_t last_read;
     uint32_t delayed_carry;
     unsigned int dma_modifier;
+    /* stereo frames handed to the frontend since the last frame end
+     * (nuubOS: whichever path handed them over) */
+    unsigned int frame_frames;
 
     struct mi_controller* mi;
     struct ri_controller* ri;
--- a/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ai/ai_controller.c
+++ b/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ai/ai_controller.c
@@ -208,6 +208,7 @@
     ai->samples_format_changed = 0;
     ai->last_read = 0;
     ai->delayed_carry = 0;
+    ai->frame_frames = 0;
 }
 
 /* Hand the backend everything the DAC has clocked out of the current
@@ -241,6 +242,7 @@
     if (length < 4)
         return;
 
+    ai->frame_frames += length / 4;
     push_audio_samples_via_libretro(
         (unsigned char*)ai->ri->rdram->dram + start + diff, length);
 }
@@ -332,9 +334,22 @@
 {
     unsigned int divider = 1 + ai->regs[AI_DACRATE_REG];
     unsigned int want;
+    unsigned int handed;
 
-    if (ai->fifo[0].duration != 0
-            && ai_hand_over_played(ai, get_remaining_dma_length(ai)) != 0)
+    if (ai->fifo[0].duration != 0)
+        ai_hand_over_played(ai, get_remaining_dma_length(ai));
+    handed = ai->frame_frames;
+    ai->frame_frames = 0;
+
+    /* nuubOS: a transfer still playing hands its samples over as the DAC
+     * clocks them; silence stands only for a DAC that ran dry, and only
+     * for the part of the field nothing was handed over for.  This used to
+     * add a whole field of silence whenever nothing new had played since
+     * the last AI_LEN read, so a game polling AI_LEN (Mischief Makers)
+     * got its samples and a field of silence on top: up to 595 frames a
+     * 441-frame field, and the frontend, pacing on audio, ran it at 44 of
+     * its 50 fps. */
+    if (ai->regs[AI_STATUS_REG] & AI_STATUS_BUSY)
         return;
 
     /* Nothing was clocked out this frame: either the game has queued no
@@ -352,6 +367,6 @@
         return;
 
     want = ai->vi->delay / divider;
-    if (want != 0)
-        push_audio_silence_via_libretro(want);
+    if (want > handed)
+        push_audio_silence_via_libretro(want - handed);
 }
